Devices with an ITO/ETL/perovskite/spiro/Au planar structure based on these two ETLs (Figure S9, Supporting Information) were fabricated. The cross-sectional SEM image of the complete device is shown in Figure 3a. The thickness of the ETL, perovskite film, Spiro, and electrode are \({\approx}30\) , 700, 200, and \(80\;\mathrm{nm}\) , respectively.

Figure 3b shows the reverse and forward \(J{-}V\) scans of the devices. The device based on \(\mathrm{In}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}\) shows the lowest performance with a short-circuit current density \((J_{\mathrm{SC}})\) of \(24.10\,\mathrm{mA\,cm}^{-2}\) , \(V_{\mathrm{OC}}\) of \(1.10~\mathrm{V},\) fill factor (FF) of \(72.52\%\) , and PCE of \(19.21\%\) , \(\mathsf{S n O}_{2}\) ETL-based devices have a typical \(J_{\mathrm{SC}}\) of \(24.26~\mathrm{mA~cm}^{-2}\) , \(V_{\mathrm{OC}}\) of \(1.13\,\mathrm{~V},\) FF of \(78.14\%\) , and PCE of \(21.42\%\) (reverse scanning). By introducing \(\mathrm{In}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}\) , the performance of devices can be improved significantly. Further characterization shows that the optimum concentration of \(\mathrm{In}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}\) precursor solution is \(0.05\,\mathrm{~M~}\) (Figure S10 and Table S1, Supporting Information).

Devices based on \(\mathrm{In}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{3}/\mathrm{SnO}_{2}\) ETL show a \(J_{\mathrm{SC}}\) of \(24.53\;\mathrm{mA}\,\mathrm{cm}^{-2}\) , \(V_{\mathrm{OC}}\) of \(1.16\mathrm{~V},\) FF of \(81.23\%\) , and PCE of \(23.07\%\) with negligible hysteresis (Table 1). Therefore, our devices have good reproducibility. As shown in Figure S11 (Supporting Information), 60 devices with different ETLs were fabricated. The PCEs of devices based on \(\mathsf{S n O}_{2}\) ETL range from \(18.60\%\) to \(21.17\%\) ,

